00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:52.110
Number 5: References to locations from the
book.

00:00:52.110 --> 00:00:56.629
Stephen King’s novel, It, comes in at over
1100 pages long, making it impossible to fit

00:00:56.629 --> 00:00:58.670
every scene into the adaptation.

00:00:58.670 --> 00:01:02.399
Many of the scenes that were not included
are referenced via easter eggs, like the intersection

00:01:02.399 --> 00:01:06.770
of Witcham and Jackson where Georgie loses
an arm, which is also the exact spot a home

00:01:06.770 --> 00:01:10.770
in the old Derry township was burned to the
ground in 1741.

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:14.220
Tracker Bros Trucking was truck depot where
the kids of Derry liked to play baseball,

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:17.610
which Eddie revisits and faces manifestations
of It as an adult.

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:21.840
Ben’s school project is the Derry Standpipe,
and when he drops it, it becomes dislodged

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:23.000
from the ground.

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:26.820
This is where Stan has his first encounter
with It, and the location where some kids

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:28.630
had drowned in Derry’s past.

00:01:28.630 --> 00:01:33.300
He can also briefly be seen going through
memorial park which is adjacent to the standpipe

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:37.110
and a victim of It named Stephen Johnson turns
up there in the adult era.

00:01:37.110 --> 00:01:40.900
Beverly’s father works maintenance at the
Derry Home Hospital, where many residents

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:45.100
of Derry were born and where the younger brother
of Edward Corcoran dies.

00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:48.890
Richie sports a shirt for Freese’s department
store, a business that he runs into in the

00:01:48.890 --> 00:01:51.750
book to take refuge from an angry Henry Bowers.

00:01:51.750 --> 00:01:55.380
The Black Spot is briefly touched on in the
movie, it was nightclub that was burned down

00:01:55.380 --> 00:01:57.690
by an evil cult in Derry’s past.

00:01:57.690 --> 00:02:00.050
That brings me to another tragedy of old Derry.

00:02:00.050 --> 00:02:02.040
Number 4: The Bradley Gang Mural.

00:02:02.040 --> 00:02:06.140
As the Losers try to get some medical supplies
for Ben, he and Richie stay out in the alley

00:02:06.140 --> 00:02:10.069
where there’s a huge mural depicting one
of the stories told about Derry’s past in

00:02:10.069 --> 00:02:11.069
the novel.

00:02:11.069 --> 00:02:14.469
The Bradley gang was a group of gangsters
wanted for bank robbery and murder who had

00:02:14.469 --> 00:02:16.810
come to Derry in 1929.

00:02:16.810 --> 00:02:20.489
Practically the whole town came together to
shoot up the gang’s car, and witnesses recall

00:02:20.489 --> 00:02:23.170
a circus clown joining in on the carnage.

00:02:23.170 --> 00:02:27.160
Although Pennywise isn’t seen initially
in the painting, It has the ability to manipulate

00:02:27.160 --> 00:02:31.569
the town, and shortly after the clown can
be seen watching them in the alleyway...

00:02:31.569 --> 00:02:34.400
Speaking of clowns, there are a lot of secrets
hidden in…

00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:36.680
Number 3: The Clown Room.

00:02:36.680 --> 00:02:41.430
Richie wanders into this room inside 29 Neibolt
Street where he’s faced with his worst fear.

00:02:41.430 --> 00:02:42.430
“Clowns”.

00:02:42.430 --> 00:02:46.430
I’ve already discussed this reference to
the TV mini-series adaptation of It, but in

00:02:46.430 --> 00:02:50.129
addition to that, there’s a clown statue
that turns it’s head, this picture that

00:02:50.129 --> 00:02:54.189
I just find particularly creepy, and the model
Richie finds of himself which matches his

00:02:54.189 --> 00:02:56.660
earlier prediction about what happened to
Betty Ripsom.

00:02:56.660 --> 00:02:58.480
“You think they’ll actually find her?”

00:02:58.480 --> 00:03:02.579
“Sure, in a ditch all decomposed covered
in worms and maggots, smelling like Eddie's

00:03:02.579 --> 00:03:03.579
Mom's underwear.”

00:03:03.579 --> 00:03:04.579
"Shut up!"

00:03:04.579 --> 00:03:05.939
Number 2: The Turtle

00:03:05.939 --> 00:03:10.170
Millions of years ago when It was created
by the celestial force known as “The Other”,

00:03:10.170 --> 00:03:15.749
another entity was also created, and this
was The Turtle, essentially the rival of It.

00:03:15.749 --> 00:03:19.580
The Turtle subtly pops up here and there in
the book to help the Losers Club, and there

00:03:19.580 --> 00:03:23.700
are a couple of similar references in the
movie, like the LEGO turtle that Bill finds

00:03:23.700 --> 00:03:28.750
in Georgie’s room, the model of the walkie
talkies that they use, TRTL 500, and the turtle

00:03:28.750 --> 00:03:31.359
that touches Richie’s foot in the quarry.

00:03:31.360 --> 00:03:33.080
“It’s a turtle.”

00:03:35.409 --> 00:03:38.900
Number 1: The cosmic origins of It.

00:03:38.910 --> 00:03:42.889
This isn’t really explored in the movie,
but the novel alludes to It and The Turtle

00:03:42.889 --> 00:03:48.310
being the original inhabitants of an outer-dimensional
void known as the macroverse, and in one scene,

00:03:48.310 --> 00:03:51.109
we see It crash landing on earth from outer
space.

00:03:51.109 --> 00:03:56.249
However, fans of the book will be pleased
to see some small nods to It’s cosmic origins,

00:03:56.249 --> 00:04:00.859
like the solar system setup in Bill’s room,
the reach for the stars poster in the library,

00:04:00.859 --> 00:04:05.540
the moon poster and globes seen in Ben’s
room, the alien spaceship found in Georgie’s

00:04:05.540 --> 00:04:08.829
room and Ben’s shirt during the projector
and Neibolt scenes.

00:04:08.829 --> 00:04:12.139
These have been the Top 5 Things You Missed
in IT.

